# Wanderlust MERN Application — Docker & AWS EC2 Deployment Documentation

**Repository:** https://github.com/iamajaypokharel/wanderlust-Devops-mern  
**Branch:** `main`  
**Deployment model:** Docker containers on a single AWS EC2 instance  
**Container orchestration:** Docker CLI (no Docker Compose required for the deployed workflow)  
**Application:** Wanderlust travel blog (MERN stack)

---

## 1. Project Overview

Wanderlust is a MERN-based travel blog application. The application contains a React/Vite frontend, a Node.js/Express backend, and a MongoDB database.

The original application is designed as an open-source travel blog and includes features such as featured travel posts, category-based discovery, user-oriented navigation, authentication, and post-related API functionality.

This deployment project adds the DevOps layer needed to run the application on AWS EC2 using Docker containers.

### Main goals of this deployment

1. Containerize the frontend, backend, and MongoDB components.
2. Run each application component as an independent Docker container.
3. Connect the containers through a user-defined Docker bridge network.
4. Persist MongoDB data using a Docker volume.
5. Import the supplied sample travel-post data automatically into MongoDB.
6. Publish the frontend and backend ports from the EC2 host.
7. Configure CORS and backend MongoDB connectivity for the EC2 environment.
8. Store the application source in GitHub for version control and future CI/CD.

