## 8. Docker Network

Create the application network once:

```bash
docker network create mern-network
```

Verify:

```bash
docker network ls
```

Inspect it:

```bash
docker network inspect mern-network
```

The three containers should appear on the same network:

```text
mern-frontend
mern-backend
mern-mongo
```

### Why a user-defined network is used

A user-defined Docker bridge network provides Docker DNS-based name resolution between containers. This makes:

```text
mongo
```

resolvable from the backend without hard-coding the MongoDB container IP address.

This is more reliable than using a dynamic container IP such as `172.19.0.x`.

