## 10. AWS EC2 Configuration

The application is deployed to an AWS EC2 Ubuntu server.

For testing, the EC2 security group should allow the required application ports.

### Recommended inbound rules for the current learning deployment

| Protocol | Port | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| TCP | 22 | SSH administration |
| TCP | 5173 | React/Vite frontend |
| TCP | 5000 | Express backend |

MongoDB port `27017` should **not** be exposed publicly for this architecture. The backend reaches MongoDB through the private Docker network.

### Accessing the application

Frontend:

```text
http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>:5173
```

Backend:

```text
http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>:5000
```

Posts API:

```text
