## 12. Rebuild and Redeploy After Code Changes

Because the deployed workflow does not use Docker Compose, each changed service can be rebuilt independently.

### Backend update

```bash
git pull

docker build -t mern-backend:latest ./backend

docker rm -f mern-backend

docker run -d \
  --name mern-backend \
  --network mern-network \
  -p 5000:5000 \
  -e PORT=5000 \
  -e MONGODB_URI="mongodb://mongo:27017/wanderlust" \
  mern-backend:latest
```

### Frontend update

```bash
git pull

docker build -t mern-frontend:latest ./frontend

docker rm -f mern-frontend

docker run -d \
  --name mern-frontend \
  --network mern-network \
  -p 5173:5173 \
  mern-frontend:latest
```

### MongoDB update

Only rebuild MongoDB when the Mongo image/Dockerfile changes:

```bash
docker build -t wanderlust-devops-mongodb:latest -f Dockerfile.mongo .
docker rm -f mern-mongo
docker run -d \
  --name mern-mongo \
  --network mern-network \
  --network-alias mongo \
  -v mongo-data:/data/db \
  wanderlust-devops-mongodb:latest
```

The `mongo-data` volume should be retained so the database survives container recreation.

