## 15. Nginx Configuration

The repository includes `nginx.conf` with an intended reverse-proxy architecture:

```text
/upstream frontend_server/  -> frontend:5173
/upstream backend_server/   -> backend:5000
```

It routes:

```text
/api/*  -> backend
/*      -> frontend
```

This is a useful next step for production because it allows the browser to communicate through one public HTTP endpoint instead of exposing the frontend and backend as separate public ports.

A target architecture is:

```text
Browser
   |
   v
EC2 :80
   |
   +---- /api/* ----> backend:5000
   |
   +---- /* --------> frontend:5173
```

For production, it is additionally recommended to serve a compiled React build using Nginx rather than keeping the Vite development server exposed on port 5173.

