## 20. Recommended Production Improvements

This project is a strong hands-on Docker/EC2 deployment, but the next improvements would make it closer to production practice.

### 20.1 Use Nginx as the single public entry point

Expose only port 80/443 and reverse proxy the frontend/API internally.

### 20.2 Serve a production React build

Replace the Vite development server with a build stage:

```bash
npm run build
```

and serve the generated static files through Nginx.

### 20.3 Use HTTPS

Add a domain name and TLS certificates, preferably with an automated certificate process.

### 20.4 Use secret management

Move JWT secrets and other confidential configuration out of Git and image layers.

### 20.5 Add container restart policies

Example:

```bash
--restart unless-stopped
```

### 20.6 Add health checks

Add HTTP and database health checks so failures can be detected automatically.

### 20.7 Build immutable versioned images

Instead of relying only on `latest`, use tags such as:

```text
mern-backend:1.0.0
mern-frontend:1.0.0
wanderlust-mongodb:1.0.0
```

### 20.8 Push images to a container registry

Docker Hub or Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) can be used so the EC2 host pulls known image versions rather than rebuilding every deployment.

### 20.9 CI/CD

A future pipeline can be:

```text
Developer
   |
   v
GitHub
   |
   v
GitHub Actions
   |
   +--> Test
   +--> Build Docker images
   +--> Scan images
   +--> Push to registry
   |
   v
EC2 deployment
   |
   +--> Pull image
   +--> Restart service
   +--> Run health checks
```

### 20.10 Monitoring and logging

Prometheus/Grafana, CloudWatch, or another monitoring stack can be added later for metrics, availability, CPU/memory monitoring, and application logs.

